  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle.\n• Thinly slice brown onion. Finely chop or crush garlic.\n• Cut tomato into wedges. Cut zucchini into rounds. Cut lemon into wedges.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-66333a32f66ba7dc6c09d363-ac784b4b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Half-fill a large saucepan with boiling water over high heat. Cook risoni in boiling water until 'al dente', 7-8 mins.Drain risoni and set aside.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-66333a32f66ba7dc6c09d363-745b7d32.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Return saucepan to medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Cook onion, tomato and zucchini until softened, 5-6 mins. Add garlic and herby tomato seasoning and cook until fragrant, 1 min.\n• Return risoni to saucepan and stir through vegetable stock.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-66333a32f66ba7dc6c09d363-eb72d24a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Stir Parmesan cheese, the butter, a squeeze of lemon juice and the baby spinach through risoni until spinach has wilted. Add a splash of water to loosen if needed.\n• Season to taste.\n• Divide risoni between bowls. Sprinkle with a pinch of chilli flakes (if using) and flaked almonds.\n• Serve with lemon wedges.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-66333a32f66ba7dc6c09d363-45c866be.jpeg"
    }
  ]
